    following XXIV Conference of PhD Students and Young Scientists.
  </p>
  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>
    The security of your Personal Information is important to us, however, please remember that no method of
    transmission over the Internet, or method of electronic storage, is 100% secure. While we strive to use commercially
    acceptable means to protect your Personal Information, we cannot guarantee its absolute security.
  </p>
  <p>
    Converetti is not legally responsible for any data security breaches that may occur in case of external data
    security threats, such as cyberattacks or other unforeseen external events associated with cyberattacks.
  </p>
  <p>
    Please note, we do not make a security backup of your data during the data-processing
    period. Therefore, in an unlikely event of a security breach and subsequent full
    database deletion (according to our security procedure) we will not be able to restore
    your erased data.
  </p>
  <h2>What are your data protection rights?</h2>
  <p>
    We would like to make sure you are fully aware of all of your data protection rights. Every user is entitled to the
    following:
  </p>
  <p>
    <b>The right to access</b> - You have the right to request “Converetti” for copies of your personal data. We may
    charge you a small fee for this service.<br />
    <b>The right to rectification</b> - You have the right to request that “Converetti” correct any information you
    believe is inaccurate. You also have the right to request “Converetti” to complete the information you believe is
    incomplete.<br />
    <b>The right to erasure</b> - You have the right to request that we erase your personal data.<br />
    <b>The right to restrict processing</b> - You have the right to request that “Converetti” restrict the processing of
    your personal data.<br />
    <b>The right to object to processing</b> - You have the right to object to “Converetti” processing of your personal
    data for reasons related to your particular situation, in accordance with Article 21 of the GDPR.<br />
    <b>The right to data portability</b> - You have the right to request that “Converetti” transfer the data that we
    have collected to another organisation, or directly to you.<br />
    <b>The right to withdraw consent</b> - withdraw consent to the processing of personal data by contacting us via
    email (<a href="mailto: office@converetti.com">office@converetti.com</a>) - if you have previously given such
    consent and the processing of your data is based on it.<br />
  </p>
  <p>
    If you make a request, we have one month to respond to your request. If you would like to exercise any of these
    rights, please contact us at our email: <a href="mailto: office@converetti.com">office@converetti.com</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    Regardless of the above, you have the right to lodge a complaint with the supervisory authority, i.e., the President
    of the Office for the Protection of Personal Data (ul. Stawki 2, 00-193 Warsaw), if you believe that the processing
    of your personal data violates the provisions of the GDPR.
  </p>
